20:["$","p","Intrusive thoughts themselves are universal. What distinguishes OCD is the meaning attached to them — the sense that having the thought says something about who you are, and that certainty must be obtained.",{"className":"text-base leading-relaxed text-body","children":"Intrusive thoughts themselves are universal. What distinguishes OCD is the meaning attached to them — the sense that having the thought says something about who you are, and that certainty must be obtained."}]
21:["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-3xl border border-line bg-surface p-6","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-serif text-xl text-ink","children":"Symptom mechanics"}],[["$","p","A compulsion works. Checking the lock, seeking reassurance, or repeating a phrase genuinely lowers anxiety in the moment, which teaches the brain that the danger was real and the ritual saved you.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"A compulsion works. Checking the lock, seeking reassurance, or repeating a phrase genuinely lowers anxiety in the moment, which teaches the brain that the danger was real and the ritual saved you."}],["$","p","Exposure and Response Prevention breaks that lesson. You approach the trigger and deliberately do not perform the ritual, so the brain learns that discomfort falls on its own. Anxiety habituates; certainty never arrives, and stops being required.",{"className":"mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body","children":"Exposure and Response Prevention breaks that lesson. You approach the trigger and deliberately do not perform the ritual, so the brain learns that discomfort falls on its own. Anxiety habituates; certainty never arrives, and stops being required."}]]]}]
